## Control {{controlId}}: Develop and Implement Plans of Action (POA&M) to Correct Deficiencies

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization develops and implements Plans of Action and Milestones within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through documented system interconnection inventory and connection authorization procedures described in "System Interconnection Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

**System Interconnection Inventory:**
The organization maintains a "System Interconnection Inventory Document" documenting all internal system connections:
- M365 GCC High tenant connections (Exchange Online, SharePoint, Teams, Intune, Defender)
- Azure Government resource connections (if applicable)
- On-premises to cloud hybrid connections (Azure AD Connect, mail flow connectors)
- Third-party application integrations (registered in Entra ID enterprise applications)

{{#if crossTenantPolicyConfigured}}
**Cross-Tenant Connections:**
Cross-tenant access policies govern external B2B connections, providing supporting evidence for interconnection authorization. External collaboration is restricted to explicitly authorized partner organizations.
{{/if}}

**Connection Authorization Process:**
- All system interconnections require documented authorization from {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- Interconnection Security Agreements (ISAs) required for connections with external systems
- Annual review of all system connections to verify continued authorization and security compliance
- Unauthorized connections identified and disconnected within 24 hours

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Maintain interconnection inventory; annual review of all connections; ISA renewal per schedule
- **Frequency:** Annual comprehensive review, continuous monitoring for unauthorized connections
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** System Interconnection Policy v1.0, Interconnection Inventory Register

**Review Frequency:** Annually by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine system interconnection inventory, ISA documentation, Entra ID enterprise application registrations, and cross-tenant access policy configurations.

